     Both of these are perfect examples of why NetHack deletes out of date
bones and save files.  Adding or removing either the MAIL option or the
SCORE_ON_BOTL option ends up causing changes to internal data structures,
rendering old data stored in the files into gibberish.  Feeding garbage
to the program just provokes a variety of failures, closely followed by
spurious bug reports.

     Moving/renaming out of date files instead of deleting them might be
reasonable in some cases, particularly unreliable system clocks, but it
won't solve the underlying problem.  People who choose to reconfigure and
recompile without also installing a whole new playground directory are
expected to know what they're doing, and `make update' under Unix does
automatically touch the date of any existing save files.



